  "about": "A file's format by its name (docs/dev/documents.md): gamma/documents/formats.py and frontend/src/documents/formats.js. names: both sides. name is a file name; format and language are what format_of / formatOf answer (language null when there is none); ext is the extension it is stored under (stored_extension / storedExtension: the last suffix lowercased, .bin when it has none or a malformed one), null when it is blocked (the backend raises ValueError, the client answers null). media: the backend alone, how a stored file is served: media is media_type(ext) (null when Gamma never stores that extension), inline and sandboxed whether ext is in INLINE_EXTENSIONS and SANDBOXED_EXTENSIONS. sniff: the backend alone, a name the table does not know settled by its first bytes: the bytes are pad bytes 'a' followed by head encoded as latin-1. Read by backend/tests/test_shared_fixtures.py and frontend/tests/documents.test.mjs.",
